.git
bin
# A bare `.env` matches the context ROOT only and matches no suffixed name,
# so `deploy/.env.prod` shipped into every build context the moment an
# operator created it (audit B36). The final distroless stage copies only the
# binary, so nothing reached a published image, but the builder layer held it.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.local
docs
*.md
.github
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
# Frontend build/test artifacts. portal/node_modules is ~200 MB of host
# (darwin-arm64) modules that `COPY portal/ .` would otherwise merge OVER the
# image's fresh Linux `npm ci` install — a platform-path collision CI can't
# reproduce. The rest are local-only outputs that bloat the build context.
portal/node_modules
portal/dist
portal/coverage
portal/test-results
portal/playwright-report
# Agent/tooling state and the generated marketplace tree (not copied into any
# image; the api renders its own at runtime).
.remember
.claude
marketplace
